      "content": "It can be frustrating to notice unexpected charges mid-way through your statement, but there are steps you can take to help prevent this:\n\n1. **Enable Transaction Alerts:** Set up real-time notifications for when transactions are processed. This way, you'll be immediately notified of new charges, allowing you to act quickly if there are any unauthorized transactions.\n2. **Review Statements Regularly:** Regularly reviewing your bank statements, especially at the end of each month, can help catch unexpected transactions early. Schedule a time each month specifically dedicated to this task.\n3. **Check Linked Accounts:** Ensure that all accounts are authorized for all transactions. Review linked accounts like Amazon, Apple, or your main bank to see if there’s any activity you don't recognize.\n4. **Regularly Review Subscriptions:** Keep an eye on your subscriptions and recurring payments. You can usually find these in your online bank or payment service account's account settings; periodically set aside time to review them.\n5. **Monitor Bank Alerts:** Besides transaction alerts, set up bank alerts that notify you of specific activities, such as new card issues, high balances, or several failed login attempts.\n6. **Secure Your Account Information:** Regularly update your passwords and opt for complex, unique passwords for",
